$MDESC::Type = "CTF_HamstersMaps";
$MDESC::Text = "<s3><f1>Mission Type: <f0> Capture the Flag" @
         "\n<f1>Author: <f0> Hamster_of_Doom!" @
	 "\n<f1>Questions, Comments, Pity: <f0> rvr279@home.com" @	
 	 "\n<f1>ICQ: <f0> 25400277 <f1>AIM: <f0> Rover v1" @ 
	 "\n<f1>Map Version: <f0> 1.3" @
	 "\n<f1>Updates: <f0> http://members.home.net/rvr279/hamster" @
	 "\n<f1>Map Type: <f0> Server-Side" @
	 "\n<f1>Planet: <f0> Altara Minor" @
         "\n<f1>System: <f0> Salius" @
         "\n<f1>Gravity: <f0> Normal" @ 
	 "\n<f1>Weather: <f0> Clear" @
         "\n<f1>Time of Day: <f0> Midday" @ 
         "\n<f1>Date: <f0> June 23rd, 4044" @
         "\n<f1>Campaign: <f0> Power Struggle" @         
	 "\n<f1># of Captures to Victory: <f0> 8" @
	 "\n<f1># of Teams: <f0> 2" @
	 "\n<f1>Max # of Players: <f0> 24" @
	 "\n\n<f1>Briefing:<f0> Listen up soldiers! Our enemies have stolen one of our floating Tiger Mk VI bases from our baseyard! They cannot be permitted to successfully capture it! Our engineers have disclosed a major weakness of the Tiger Mk VI -- its team-recognition technology can be altered by any soldier that knows the location of a special switch! Your squad will be assigned to another Tiger Mk VI in an attempt to recapture our stolen base. Soldiers should make any and all attempt to switch the stolen base back to our team! Additionally, if we capture the enemy's flag 8 times, we can teach them a major lesson. Make sure soldiers are assigned to guard our base's switch. We can't take the chance that our enemy has discovered the Tiger Mk VI's weakness. The loss of two of our bases would be devastating!\n\nFailure is not an option.\n\nDISMISSED!\n\n<f1>Tips:\n<f0>Grab the tech switch for your base ASAP, so your turrets will come on-line and fire at rushing opponents.\nJust like on Rollercoaster, placing deployables too close to the force-field doors could result in the them sticking in the open position.\nIf your team has lost control of both bases and is having trouble getting them back, try to get to the center ruins; there are an inv and ammo station there, useable by both teams.\nDefend any switches you control!\nThink twice about taking out the enemy's gens. If your team captures their base, they will be YOUR gens!\n\n<f1>Version History<f0>\nVers. 1.3\nMoved spawn point in from out-of-bounds.\n\nVers. 1.2\nUpdated contact info.\n\nVers. 1.1\nUpdated (.dsc) description file.\nChanged cap limit from default to 8.\n\n<f1>Thanks to:\n<f0>Shadow of Death and Tedaw for debuting my maps on their server!\nOmnipotent & others for their mapping tutorials.\nThe mapping community at large for inspiration, demonstration, and perspiration.\nAnd of course the team at Dynamix for Tribes!";